# ==============================================================================
# Demo scaffold configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed and is
# the documentation, so keep it current — tests/env-example.test.ts fails if the
# code reads a variable that is not described here.
#
# Nothing below is required to BOOT. The server starts with this file empty: it
# logs one warning per missing variable naming what that variable costs, /health
# answers 200 with a capability map, and only the routes that genuinely cannot
# work return 503. That is deliberate — a demo that dies at boot is undebuggable
# at the worst possible moment.
#
# Loaded by Node itself via `--env-file-if-exists=.env`. There is no dotenv
# dependency, so this file is parsed by Node's rules: no `export`, no shell
# interpolation, and quotes are taken literally.
# ==============================================================================


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# APP IDENTITY — set this FIRST
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Names the container, the Traefik routers, and the public hostname
# (https://<APP_NAME>.twilio.dtolb.com).
#
# WHY IT MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS: Traefik router names are GLOBAL on the dev
# box. Two clones of this scaffold both left at `scaffold` will define routers
# with the same names, and one demo silently steals the other's Twilio webhooks.
# Nothing errors. `scripts/preflight.mjs` refuses to bring up the stack while
# this is still the default.
#
# Format: lowercase, DNS-safe (letters, digits, dashes).
APP_NAME=scaffold


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWILIO CORE — all five, or no channel starts at all
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Console → Account → API keys & tokens (https://console.twilio.com).
#
# TACConfig.fromEnv() THROWS if any one of these five is missing or malformed, so
# server/config.ts validates them first and only constructs TAC once all five are
# good. Missing any → every channel is unavailable; /health shows voice:false,
# sms:false.

# Format: AC + 32 hex characters. Validated.
TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=

# Console → Account → Auth Token (click to reveal).
# ALSO used to validate the X-Twilio-Signature on every inbound webhook, so a
# wrong value here looks like "Twilio is 403-ing us" rather than a bad secret.
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Console → Account → API keys & tokens → Create API key (Standard is enough).
# Format: SK + 32 hex characters. Validated.
TWILIO_API_KEY=

# Shown ONCE when the API key above is created. Not retrievable afterwards — if
# you lost it, make a new key.
TWILIO_API_SECRET=

# The number that places and receives calls, and sends SMS.
# Format: E.164, e.g. +15551234567. Validated (a `555-1234` here is a common
# and confusing failure).
TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER=


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VOICE (ConversationRelay)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The PUBLIC host Twilio dials back into for the media WebSocket.
#
# FAILURE MODE: TACServer THROWS AT CONSTRUCTION if a voice channel is registered
# without this. It fails fast on purpose rather than 500-ing on the first call.
#
# NOT NEEDED FOR SMS — verified at T12 by booting without it. TACServer's guard is
# `voiceChannel && !voicePublicDomain`, and voiceChannel is undefined when no
# VoiceChannel was registered. So an SMS-only demo leaves this blank and /health
# correctly reports voice:false, sms:true.
#
# Format: bare host, NO SCHEME. `https://x.com` is rejected; `x.com`,
# `x.ngrok.app:8080` and `x.com/server1` are all valid.
#
# On the Traefik dev box this is `<APP_NAME>.twilio.dtolb.com` and the box already
# terminates TLS publicly — you do NOT need ngrok.
TWILIO_VOICE_PUBLIC_DOMAIN=


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORCHESTRATED MODE (Conversation Orchestrator) — required for SMS
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Console → Conversations → Orchestrator configuration.
# Format: conv_configuration_...
#
# FAILURE MODE: `new SMSChannel(tac)` THROWS with "Messaging channels require
# conversationConfigurationId" — it does NOT degrade to a no-op, so the scaffold
# guards the construction. Omitting this leaves TAC in voice-only mode (it logs
# "Voice-only mode: ... skipping Conversation Orchestrator initialization"), where
# callSid IS the conversation id and Memory, Knowledge and handoff are ALL absent
# (getMemoryClient() returns null).
TWILIO_CONVERSATION_CONFIGURATION_ID=

# Console → Studio → the flow that fronts your human queue (Flex or otherwise).
# Format: FW + 32 hex characters.
#
# FAILURE MODE: createStudioHandoffTool() THROWS AT CONSTRUCTION without this. It
# would be built per-turn inside a handler whose errors TAC swallows, which means
# DEAD AIR on a live call. The scaffold therefore omits the tool and logs once,
# rather than risking silence. Leave blank if the demo has no human handoff.
TWILIO_STUDIO_HANDOFF_FLOW_SID=

# Console → Products & services → Enterprise Knowledge → Knowledge bases.
# Format: know_knowledgebase_ + 26 lowercase alphanumerics (a Twilio Type ID, NOT
# an SID). The docs also show a "KB..." example; that shape is not what the API
# returns.
#
# Optional and genuinely optional: absent simply means no search_knowledge tool.
# Note createKnowledgeSearchTool() requires an explicit id AND name/description.
#
# You do not need the Console: `pnpm seed:knowledge` creates a base, pushes the
# Northwind Traders articles from scripts/knowledge-articles.ts, and prints the id
# to paste here. `node --env-file-if-exists=.env scripts/verify-knowledge.ts` then
# proves the content is indexed and retrievable, for free — Knowledge search is
# not billed traffic.
TWILIO_KNOWLEDGE_BASE_ID=

# One knob for TAC, TAC's Fastify logger, and our own pino instance — they all
# read this name, so there is no way for them to disagree.
# trace | debug | info | warn | error | fatal
TWILIO_LOG_LEVEL=info


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

# https://platform.openai.com/api-keys
#
# THE NAME MATTERS: @ai-sdk/openai reads exactly `OPENAI_API_KEY`. A perfectly
# good key under `OPENAI_APIKEY` is invisible to the SDK, and the resulting
# "missing key" error while the key is plainly in your .env is maddening.
#
# Verify with: node --env-file-if-exists=.env scripts/verify-model.mjs
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional override used ONLY by scripts/verify-model.mjs, to force a specific
# model when diagnosing. The agent itself does not read this — its model comes
# from the Langfuse prompt's versioned `config.model`, so that changing models is
# a prompt revision rather than a redeploy.
# Leave blank to let the diagnostic pick the best available model automatically.
MODEL=


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LANGFUSE — prompt management, tool selection, and tracing
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted per demo:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.langfuse.yml up -d
#
# FAILURE MODE (deliberately soft): if Langfuse is unreachable, prompts fall back
# to the compiled-in defaults in server/agent/prompt/defaults.ts and report their
# version as "fallback" in the console. No traces are recorded. The demo still
# runs — which matters, because this is 6 containers taking 2-3 minutes to boot.

# The scaffold's own client. Host port 3100, NOT 3000 — langfuse-web defaults to
# 3000 and would collide with `next dev`.
LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3100
LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-scaffold-local
LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-scaffold-local

# --- Headless initialization -------------------------------------------------
# These make the Langfuse stack self-provisioning: on first boot it creates the
# org, project and API keys with exactly these values, so there is no signup step
# and the keys above are deterministic and committable-as-examples.
#
# GOTCHA: do NOT wrap these in quotes. Quoted values break initialization
# (Langfuse's own troubleshooting note).
#
# The two key values MUST match LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY / LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY above.
LANGFUSE_INIT_ORG_ID=demo
LANGFUSE_INIT_ORG_NAME=Demo
LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_ID=scaffold
LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_NAME=Scaffold
LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_PUBLIC_KEY=pk-lf-scaffold-local
LANGFUSE_INIT_PROJECT_SECRET_KEY=sk-lf-scaffold-local
LANGFUSE_INIT_USER_EMAIL=demo@example.com
LANGFUSE_INIT_USER_NAME=Demo
LANGFUSE_INIT_USER_PASSWORD=changeme-at-least-8-chars

# Consumed by langfuse-web itself, not by our code.
# NEXTAUTH_URL must match the origin you actually browse to, or login redirects
# bounce. Use the public URL if you expose Langfuse through Traefik.
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=change-me
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3100


# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --- NOT set here on purpose ---
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# PORT / AGENT_PORT — deliberately NOT configurable. The port is a compile-time
#   constant in shared/ports.ts (8910) because the browser, the server and the
#   Traefik `loadbalancer.server.port` label must all agree, and an env var that
#   only some of them read is a silent 502. 8910 dodges three occupied ports:
#   8080 (Traefik's dashboard on this box), 8787 (nw-poc and aci-quality-poc),
#   and 8000 (TAC's default).
#
# TWILIO_VOICE_WEBSOCKET_PATH / TWILIO_VOICE_ACTION_PATH /
# TWILIO_VOICE_CALL_EVENT_PATH — TAC's defaults are used as-is (/ws,
#   /conversation-relay-callback, /twilio/call-events). Overriding any of them
#   silently desynchronises shared/twilio-paths.ts from the Traefik PathPrefix
#   labels, and the symptom is a 404 that looks like a Twilio problem.
#   tests/architecture.test.ts asserts the two agree.
#
# CORP_CA_PATH — passed on the command line at build time, not stored here:
#   CORP_CA_PATH="$HOME/.config/zscaler-root.crt" docker compose up -d --build
#   Set it to /dev/null when off the corporate VPN.
#
# TWILIO_REGION — add it only if the account is region-pinned.
#
# TWILIO_TAC_CI_* (Conversation Intelligence) — not wired in this scaffold.
